 "source": {
  "map": "Map 5, Areas of Special Concern (page 42 of Washington County, Bethany Community Plan, Chapter 1 text and maps (chapter-1-bethany-community-plan-text-and-maps-09-2026), https://washingtoncountyor.gov/lut/planning/documents/chapter-1-bethany-community-plan-text-and-maps-09-2026/download, retrieved 2026-10-30, sha256 6ff194eff86183d736865722d72e9be2852fee105266f5d30810d1165ae91851; the sheet is printed 2/9/2023), the outline of ASC 1 (Central Bethany).",
  "quote": "or/washington/_unincorporated/community-plan.bethany.txt#L870-L872,L876-L877,L1035-L1037",
  "inputs": {
   "taxlots": "Washington County taxlots FeatureServer (gispub.co.washington.or.us/server/rest/services/Washington_County_Taxlots/FeatureServer/0), envelope 7600900,695300 to 7605700,697700 EPSG:2913, fetched 2026-10-30, 1324 lots, sha256 a4edea2dd847a103...",
   "zoning": "Washington County Land Use Districts (gispub.co.washington.or.us LUT_PDS/Planning_Layers/MapServer/0), same envelope, fetched 2026-10-30; a lot takes the district covering most of it",
   "streets": "Washington County street centrelines (gispub.co.washington.or.us LUT_PDS/Base_Layers/MapServer/1), fetched 2026-10-30"
  },
  "traced_by": "Claude (bethany-asc worker, FOLLOWUPS 130)",
  "traced_on": "2026-10-30",
  "drawn": true,
  "how": "The sheet is an ArcGIS Pro GeoPDF: the Areas_of_Special_Concern map frame carries a /VP viewport with its CRS (NAD_1983_HARN_StatePlane_Oregon_North_FIPS_3601, feet = EPSG:2913) and its corner coordinates; the page-to-ground affine was fitted to them (residual 0.89 ft) and the map's own vector paths were read out of the page, so nothing was rendered, picked or flood-filled. The Areas of Special Concern are closed outlines filled pink (RGB 1, 0.745, 0.745) and stroked red. The map's numerals are in a font the page does not decode, so ASC 1 is named by what it holds: the one outline that takes in both southern quadrants of the Bethany Boulevard / Laidlaw Road intersection (its corner lies 11.6 ft outside, on the Laidlaw right-of-way), the Community Business District of Bethany Village at the southeast quadrant and Parcels 1 and 2 of ASC 1A at the southwest, as the text places them (#L911-L912, L894-L896), and all five outlines of ASC 1A, which the text sets inside ASC 1 (its 155 dwellings are 'out of the required 860' of ASC 1, #L1042, L1050-L1051). Checked by laying the county's current taxlots over it: the outline runs on lot and right-of-way lines, cutting one lot of the 748 it reaches. A lot the outline cuts carries the flag too (ruling 2026-10-30-bethany-asc1-green-with-flag: the flag sits below the yellow line, so carrying it on a lot half inside costs nothing, and dropping it would hide the question): the one cut lot, 1N120DA20300 (39 percent inside), is added whole to the outline. A lot 10 percent or less inside is outside, as the drawn reading takes it.",
